  <prompt>
    Build a SemanticAppendixGenerator for the compose-document scope (defined terms, cross-references, structural metadata appended to the scope payload) and measure the LLM hallucination delta WITH vs WITHOUT the appendix over the same set of document questions/edits. This validates that the appendix reduces hallucination before FR-22 (task 023) builds the production generator + CriticMarkup read-direction rendering. Deliverable is a spike note recording the measured delta + the appendix content format.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI platform developer measuring LLM grounding/hallucination, familiar with adeu's Semantic Appendix pattern and the ADR-039 grounded-output invariant.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A spike note at projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/spike-4-semantic-appendix.md that unlocks the FR-22 decision: hallucination-reduction validation — a measured WITH-vs-WITHOUT delta over a fixed question/edit set, plus the appendix content format (defined terms, cross-refs, structural metadata) to reproduce in production.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §6.1 (Semantic Appendix in scope payload) + §13 Spike 4 + spec FR-22. The appendix gives the LLM defined terms, cross-references, and structural metadata so it hallucinates less. This spike measures the delta before task 023 builds SemanticAppendixGenerator + CriticMarkup read-direction rendering for the compose-document scope. Decision unlocked (design §13): hallucination-reduction validation.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="target-service-dir">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ — where production SemanticAppendixGenerator lands (task 023); spike prototypes under notes/spikes/</file>
      <file purpose="dispatch-seam">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/dispatchConsumer.ts — reuse the confirmed seam to run the A/B invocations</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">No task dependencies — startable immediately (Wave W0).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">The appendix enriches a scope payload consumed by a grounded LLM invocation; the spike honors the grounded-output invariant and dispatches via the shipped seam (no new endpoint).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Services/Compose code (incl. the appendix generator) MUST NOT inject AI internals; the generator produces a payload, it does not call the model directly. Tier-1 NetArchTest enforces this in production.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Throwaway generator + measurement — production service is FR-22 (task 023); deliverable is a spike note under notes/spikes/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ai/grounding, ai/semantic-appendix, ai/hallucination-measurement</topic>
    <files>
